.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt ARCANA-AGENT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcana-agent
.Nd serve the jails of this host to arcana clients
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dF
.Op Fl A Ar cafile
.Op Fl C Ar certfile
.Op Fl K Ar keyfile
.Op Fl D Ar confdir
.Op Fl f Ar jail.conf
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl j Ar jail
.Op Fl l Ar uri
.Op Fl p Ar pidfile
.Op Fl R Ar rc.d dirs
.Op Fl s Ar service
.Op Fl y Ar sysrc
.Op Fl U Ar program
.Op Fl B Ar dir
.Op Fl c Ar config.mk
.Op Fl G Ar git
.Op Fl M Ar make
.Op Fl I Ar ifconfig
.Op Fl r Ar route
.Op Fl n Ar ngctl
.Op Fl k Ar wg
.Op Fl o Ar directory
.Op Fl b Ar birdc
.Op Fl e Ar bird
.Op Fl a Ar file
.Op Fl L Ar jls
.Op Fl x Ar jexec
.Op Fl T Ar kldload
.Op Fl t Ar kldunload
.Op Fl z Ar zfs
.Op Fl q Ar gpart
.Op Fl i Ar camcontrol
.Op Fl m Ar mount
.Op Fl u Ar umount
.Op Fl S Ar fstab
.Op Fl Q Ar sysctl
.Op Fl O Ar sysctl.conf
.Op Fl H Ar helper
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Op Fl N Ar netstat
.Op Fl X Ar sockstat
.Op Fl W Ar swapinfo
.Op Fl Z Ar zpool
.Op Fl P Ar pkg
.Nm
.Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the
.Ql arcana
cblink family: it reports the jails of this host and changes them for
clients such as the arcana web console and
.Xr arcanactl 8 .
It is the only privileged part of arcana.
.Pp
Running jails are read with
.Xr jail_getv 3
and their processes with
.Xr libprocstat 3 .
Configured jails are read with
.Ql jail -f file -e
for
.Pa /etc/jail.conf
and every
.Pa /etc/jail.conf.d/*.conf
that
.Pa /etc/jail.conf
does not include, the files
.Pa /etc/rc.d/jail
would use, so variables, includes and shared statements mean what they
mean to
.Xr jail 8 .
.Pp
Starting, stopping and restarting run
.Xr jail 8
with
.Fl c ,
.Fl r
or
.Fl rc
and the file that defines the jail, so the jail's
.Va exec.*
hooks, mounts and interfaces are handled as usual.
Killing removes the jail with
.Xr jail_remove 2 .
Addresses change in the running jail with
.Xr jail_setv 3
and, when the jail has an
.Va interface ,
an alias added or removed on it; in the configuration they change in
place with libjailconf, as
.Xr jailconf 8
does.
The previous file is kept as
.Pa file.arcana.bak ,
and if
.Xr jail 8
does not read the new file as intended it is put back.
.Pp
Beyond jails it reports and changes the host itself, always through the
system's own programs.
Services are the executable scripts of
.Pa /etc/rc.d
and
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d :
whether they are enabled is read from
.Ql sysrc -A ,
whether the enabled ones run from
.Ql service name status ;
they are started, stopped, restarted and reloaded with
.Xr service 8 ,
enabled and disabled, and their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables read and set, with
.Xr sysrc 8 .
The routing table, the nexthops, the active connections and the open
sockets are what
.Xr netstat 1
and
.Xr sockstat 1
print with
.Fl -libxo Cm json ,
one run per address family.
Usage figures are the CPU share from
.Va kern.cp_time
between two requests, memory from the
.Va vm.stats.vm
counters, swap from
.Xr swapinfo 8
and the ZFS pools from
.Xr zpool 8 .
Packages that the repository has newer versions of are listed with
.Ql pkg version -vRl '<'
and upgraded with
.Ql pkg upgrade -y ,
on the host or, with
.Ql pkg -j ,
in a running jail.
.Pp
Every reply carries a trace: the library calls, system calls, files and
programs the request used, with the output of every program.
Changes are made one at a time; reading is not held up by them.
.Pp
Every operation requires an authenticated peer.
On a local socket that is anyone who can open it: the socket is mode
0600, or 0660 with
.Fl g .
On the network it is a peer with a client certificate issued by
.Ar cafile ,
over TLS 1.3.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A Ar cafile
Certificate authority for client certificates.
.It Fl C Ar certfile , Fl K Ar keyfile
This server's certificate and key.
The three files are read at startup, before the daemon detaches: one
that is missing, unreadable, not PEM, or a key that is not the
certificate's, is an error that names the file.
.It Fl D Ar confdir
Per-jail configuration files.
Default
.Pa /etc/jail.conf.d .
.It Fl d
Log debugging messages.
.It Fl F
Stay in the foreground and log to standard error.
.It Fl f Ar jail.conf
Main configuration file.
Default
.Pa /etc/jail.conf .
.It Fl g Ar group
Make local sockets mode 0660 and owned by
.Ar group .
.It Fl j Ar jail
The
.Xr jail 8
program.
.It Fl l Ar uri
Listen on
.Ar uri ,
which may be given up to eight times:
.Ql unix:/path ,
.Ql tcp://address:port
or
.Ql sctp://address[,address ...]:port .
Network listeners need
.Fl A ,
.Fl C
and
.Fl K .
Default
.Ql unix:/var/run/arcana-agent.sock .
Beside every
.Ql tcp://
listener
.Nm
listens on SCTP at the same address and port, where the kernel has
SCTP.
It does not load the
.Xr sctp 4
module, and where it is missing does not try again by itself: it is
told to with the
.Cm transport
operation, as
.Xr arcanactl 8
.Cm transport retry
does.
.It Fl p Ar pidfile
Default
.Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.pid .
.It Fl R Ar rc.d dirs
The directories whose scripts are the host's services, colon separated.
Default
.Pa /etc/rc.d:/usr/local/etc/rc.d .
.It Fl s Ar service
The
.Xr service 8
program, which lists, queries and changes services.
.It Fl y Ar sysrc
The
.Xr sysrc 8
program, which reads and writes their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables.
.It Fl U Ar program
The file an update replaces.
The default is the running program.
.It Fl B Ar dir
Where a tree is cloned and built.
Default
.Pa /var/cache/arcana-build .
.It Fl c Ar config.mk
This host's settings for a build, copied into the tree when the file
exists.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/config.mk .
.It Fl G Ar git , Fl M Ar make
The
.Xr git 1
and
.Xr make 1
programs.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl w Ar seconds
How long a change made in safe mode waits to be confirmed.
Default 60.
.It Fl I Ar ifconfig , Fl r Ar route , Fl n Ar ngctl , Fl k Ar wg , Fl b Ar birdc
The
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr route 8 ,
.Xr ngctl 8 ,
.Xr wg 8
and
.Xr birdc 8
programs.
.It Fl e Ar bird , Fl a Ar file
The
.Xr bird 8
program, which parses a configuration before it is put in place, and
BIRD's main configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/bird.conf .
.It Fl z Ar zfs , Fl q Ar gpart , Fl i Ar camcontrol , Fl m Ar mount , Fl u Ar umount
The programs storage is read and changed with:
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr camcontrol 8 ,
.Xr mount 8
and
.Xr umount 8 .
.Xr zpool 8
is
.Fl Z .
.It Fl S Ar fstab
The
.Xr fstab 5
read, and edited.
Default:
.Pa /etc/fstab .
.It Fl Q Ar sysctl , Fl O Ar sysctl.conf
The
.Xr sysctl 8
program, which sets a variable of the kernel's state, and the
.Xr sysctl.conf 5
that keeps one for the next boot.
Default:
.Pa /sbin/sysctl
and
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf .
.It Fl T Ar kldload , Fl t Ar kldunload
The
.Xr kldload 8
and
.Xr kldunload 8
programs, which load a kernel module and unload one.
.It Fl L Ar jls , Fl x Ar jexec
The
.Xr jls 8
and
.Xr jexec 8
programs: the first says whether a jail runs with a network of its own
and where its root is, the second runs the jail's own programs in it.
.It Fl H Ar helper
The program run to look at a jail's interfaces from inside it.
Default: this program itself.
.It Fl o Ar directory
Where WireGuard interfaces are written for
.Xr wg-quick 8 .
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/wireguard .
.It Fl N Ar netstat , Fl X Ar sockstat
The
.Xr netstat 1
and
.Xr sockstat 1
programs, run with
.Fl -libxo Cm json
for the network tables.
.It Fl W Ar swapinfo , Fl Z Ar zpool
The
.Xr swapinfo 8
and
.Xr zpool 8
programs, for the usage figures; a host without ZFS reports no pools.
.It Fl P Ar pkg
The
.Xr pkg 8
program, for pending upgrades and upgrading, on the host and with
.Fl j
in running jails.
Upgrades may run for up to an hour.
.El
.Sh ITS OWN SERVICE
A stop or restart of
.Nm arcana_agent
asked of the daemon itself, as a service action, is not run and waited
for as other services' are:
.Xr service 8
would wait for the daemon to stop while the daemon waits for it to end.
It is handed to a process of its own, the request is answered, and the
daemon is stopped by that process a moment later.
.Sh STOPPING
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
as from
.Ql service arcana_agent stop ,
the daemon stops.
A change that is under way is not cut short: the daemon logs what it
is and which jobs wait behind it, starts nothing more, and stops when
the change has ended, reporting again every 30 seconds while it waits.
The jobs that had not started are lost.
A second signal stops it at once, and the log says what was cut short.
A program a change had started keeps running in that case.
.Sh INTERFACES
The network interfaces are read with
.Xr getifaddrs 3
and a few ioctls, as
.Xr ifconfig 8
reads them: flags, link state, MTU, hardware address, description, the
two ends of a tunnel, counters and addresses.
They are changed by jobs that run
.Xr ifconfig 8 :
an address added as an alias or taken off, an interface brought up or
down.
Static routes are added and deleted by jobs that run
.Xr route 8 .
The changes are live only.
.Pp
A job of these kinds may ask for safe mode.
The change is made, and the job waits, in the state
.Li unconfirmed ,
for the client to confirm it; reaching the daemon again is the point.
Without that within the wait
.Pq Fl w , 60 seconds
the daemon undoes the change, as it also does when it is stopped while
waiting: an address is put back with the prefix length it had, an
interface brought back up or down, a route deleted or added again.
.Sh BUILDS
A client may ask for
.Nm
to be built from a git repository: the console does when
.Va agent_source
is set, and
.Xr arcanactl 8
with
.Cm agent-build .
The repository is cloned afresh, without history, into the build
directory, and
.Pa lib/libjailconf
and
.Pa usr.sbin/arcana-agent
are built there with
.Xr make 1 .
When the daemon is root, git and make run as
.Li nobody .
For a repository reached over SSH, the server's host key is never
taken on trust: until the client sends back the keys a person
confirmed, the reply carries the keys the server showed and their
fingerprints, and nothing is built.
Confirmed keys are kept in
.Pa known_hosts
in the build directory and checked strictly from then on.
git shows the server a key of this host's, made on first use as
.Pa id_ed25519
there, or the one the client names.
The program is sent back with its SHA-256 and the version it reports;
nothing is installed.
One build runs at a time.
.Pp
With
.Cm console-update
the whole tree is built, as the unprivileged user, and installed with
.Ql make install
as the daemon; the
.Nm arcana_console
service is restarted after the reply.
That is how a console updates itself, through the agent of its host.
.Sh UPDATES
A client may send a new
.Nm :
the console does, and
.Xr arcanactl 8
with
.Cm agent-update .
The program is checked against the SHA-256 sent with it, written beside
the installed one, and run with
.Fl V ;
one that does not run on this host is dropped.
It then takes the place of the installed program, which is kept with
the suffix
.Pa .old .
When asked to, the daemon has
.Xr service 8
restart
.Nm arcana_agent
after it has replied; jobs still queued are lost, one that is running
ends first.
.Sh RC.CONF VARIABLES
The service
.Nm arcana_agent
always listens on its local socket; network listeners are added to it.
.Bl -tag -width "arcana_agent_listen"
.It Va arcana_agent_enable
Run the agent.
.It Va arcana_agent_socket
The local socket.
Default
.Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.sock .
.It Va arcana_agent_group
A group whose members may use the socket
.Pq Fl g .
Default: none, root only.
.It Va arcana_agent_listen
Network listeners, separated by spaces, such as
.Ql tcp://0.0.0.0:4310 tcp://[::]:4310 .
Default: none.
.It Va arcana_agent_ca , arcana_agent_cert , arcana_agent_key
The files for
.Fl A ,
.Fl C
and
.Fl K ,
used when there are network listeners.
Default:
.Pa ca.pem ,
.Pa host.pem
and
.Pa host.key
in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
.It Va arcana_agent_flags
More flags, added to those the variables above give.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.sock
.It Pa /var/run/arcana-agent.pid
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Serve the console host over TLS and local tools over the default
socket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# arcana-agent -A /usr/local/etc/arcana/ca.pem \e
    -C /usr/local/etc/arcana/host.pem \e
    -K /usr/local/etc/arcana/host.key \e
    -l unix:/var/run/arcana-agent.sock \e
    -l tcp://0.0.0.0:4310 -l 'tcp://[::]:4310'
.Ed
